                <pb facs="0509" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg501"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10087: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-18T21:00:00+03:00">April 18, 1941—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 19—12:03 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. Sea-borne British troops arrived Basrah and air-borne at Shaiba today without
                    incident.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
